Build requirements -- Solaris on SPARC
======================================

Packages
--------
Solaris 10 1/13 (s10u11), installed with the SUNWCall (Entire Distribution) or
SUNWCXall (Entire Distribution plus OEM support) cluster. Packages, and what
they provide:

    SUNWgmake                   gmake, /usr/sfw/bin/gmake
    SUNWflexlex                 flex, /usr/sfw/bin/flex
    SUNWbinutils                gobjcopy, /usr/sfw/bin/gobjcopy
    SUNWgpch                    gpatch, /usr/bin/gpatch (not /usr/bin/patch)
    SUNWsprot + patch 118683-15 /usr/ccs/bin/as (see Assembler below)
    base OS                     /usr/ccs/bin/make, ld, size, mcs (SUNWbtool;
                                the hv build strips Sun cc's debug stubs from
                                its objects with it); /usr/ccs/lib/cpp
                                (traditional cpp); /usr/bin/perl
    Sun Studio                  cc, /opt/SUNWspro/bin/cc, or any other Sun
                                compiler in a different path (tested with:
                                build_matrix; see Compiler below)
    git (optional)              /opt/csw/bin/git, from OpenCSW; on PATH

stabs and aschk are built from src/hypervisor/src/support.

git gives the commit id and date to the build stamp (build/stamp.sh). Without
it the OpenBoot banner says "git unknown" instead of the commit id.

gmake, not Sun/SysV make: the top-level Makefile is GNU-make syntax and shells
out to /usr/ccs/bin/make for Sun's own makefiles. A sun-path build uses both.
Running `make` instead of `gmake` stops with a message that says so.
/usr/sfw/bin is not on the default PATH: add it, or give the full path
(/usr/sfw/bin/gmake).

Overrides: SUN_STUDIO=, AS_SUN=, LD_SUN=, FLEX=, PATCH=, OBJCOPY_SUN=.
Which Studio is used, and how ./configure picks it: README.configure.

./configure (optional; it runs under Solaris 10's /bin/sh) finds the Studio,
checks that its cc compiles and that as, gpatch and gobjcopy are usable, and
records what this particular cc needs: README.configure.

Whether a smaller install cluster has these packages was not checked (see
SUNWCXall above).


Compiler
--------
Sun Studio 11 (/opt/SUNWspro, cc 5.8), installed separately:
Solaris 10 6/06 Developer Tools, Update 2, file
Sol10.0606.DeveloperToolsU2.iso, https://archive.org/details/Solaris_10_0606_Dev

Built with Sun Studio 11 to Oracle Developer Studio 12.6, each a full install
in its own /opt directory: build_matrix. 12.5 and 12.6 need VIS declared on
the guest (isainfo -v lists vis): build_matrix.

The PROM's Forth engine is a 64-bit program (cc -xarch=v9), so the Studio needs
its 64-bit packages. ./configure links a 64-bit program and stops with that
message if it cannot.


Assembler
---------
The hypervisor is assembled with -xarch=v9d. Only /usr/ccs/bin/as with patch
118683-15 or later accepts it. The as on the s10u11 media (118683-07) and Sun
Studio 11's own assembler (bin/fbe, which its cc driver calls) reject it.

Take patch 118683-15 or a later revision, for example from the /patches
directory of the Oracle Developer Studio 12.6 distribution:
https://www.oracle.com/tools/developerstudio/downloads/developer-studio-jsp.html
Only the patch is required, not Studio 12.6 itself. With the patch:

    $ /usr/ccs/bin/as -V
    /usr/ccs/bin/as: Studio 12.5 Compiler Common 12.5 SunOS_sparc
        Patch 05/02/2016

`gmake hv_reset` assembles a test instruction before the build and stops with
a message if the assembler rejects it.
